id you guys both know  everything about everything  so what are you looking for tonight that  gives you an indication of how things  are gonna go the Democrats keep telling  us they have multiple ways to knit the  23 seats that they need to retake the  majorities you can look at a few early  states and get a sense of where they  might do quite well Virginia  Pennsylvania and New Jersey all three of  those if they win a majority of the  competitive races in those states  they're about halfway to the 23 before  10:00 p.m. Eastern tonight  Virginia ten just  said Washington and almost guaranteed  Democratic pickup if you believe the  polls if they win something like the  second District in Virginia down in  Norfolk then blue tsunami warnings may  be issued nationwide because that's the  kind of race that is a reach that  Republicans worry about that they could  conceivably win one of the most  important storylines tonight is not only  women on the ballot but women marching  to the polls right women voters and  women candidates I mean polls have  showed that women are walking away from  and in some cases running away from the  Republican Party so how pronounced is  that shift tonight and are women more  motivated to vote that's something that  we'll be able to see in our exit polls  and then beyond that this has been a  really extraordinary year for women  candidates 238 women on the ballot in  the house alone tonight that is a huge  uptick 167 just two years ago so right  now we've got 84 women currently serving  in the house if they have a great night  tonight they could surpass 100 a big  increase but that's still only 20-25  percent of the house women make up 51%  of the population an example of how they  could change the makeup of Congress  Pennsylvania right now has an all-male  delegation almost guaranteed that at  least one to maybe as many as five women  will join that delegation and the  president has had one constant theme  these past few weeks and that is  immigration immigration immigration if  Republicans do hold both houses will we  see immigration lips you'll see them  begin to push through as the campaign  signs say it is rally finish the wall  whether Democrats allow for that or if  there's some kind of a deal where  dreamers are legalized in the process  we'll see all right our experts edit  Nancy thank you so much continuous live  coverage of the midterm elections begins  on CBS M today at 5:00 p.m. for Central  and we'll all be here for primetime  election night special starting at 8:00  7:00 central right here on CBS

